==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|had|lang=enm}}, {{term|hed|lang=enm}}, {{term|hod|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|hād||person, individual, character, individuality, degree, rank, order, office, holy office, condition, state, nature, character, form, manner, sex, race, family, tribe, choir}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*haiduz||appearance, kind}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kāi-||light, bright, shining}}. Cognate with {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|hēd||consition, rank}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|heit||person, personality, sex, condition, quality, rank|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|heiðr|lang=non}} {{gloss|"honour, dignity"}} (whence {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|hæder||honour|lang=da}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|heder||honour|lang=sv}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|||tr=haidus|way, manner|lang=got}}. Same as {{l|en|-hood}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|had}}, {{l|en|haid}} {{qualifier|Scotland}} 
* {{l|en|hod}}, {{l|en|hode}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} [[person|Person]] (in all senses).
# {{context|obsolete|biological|lang=en}} [[sex|Sex]]; [[gender]].
# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|_|dialectal|Scotland|lang=en}} [[order|Order]]; [[estate]]; [[rank]]; [[degree]]; holy or religious orders.
# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|_|dialectal|Scotland|lang=en}} [[state|State]]; [[condition]]; [[quality]]; [[kind]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|hadien|lang=enm}}, {{term|hodien|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|hādian||to ordain, consecrate}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|hād||rank, order, office, holy office}}. See above.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|hode}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|had|ing}}

# {{context|transitive|obsolete|lang=en}} To [[ordain]]; [[consecrate]]; [[admit]] to a religious order.

